 changing frequently is  i was having a little trouble managing  every little thing sometimes when i  unload things i'll forget to unload some  certain thing or maybe i  shared access to some object somewhere  and forgot about it because there's a  lot of things that need to talk to each  other and it's not always super easy to  keep track of and one of the ways i  started tracking that was i just  basically  made sure all these values were properly  reset and you can't necessarily  necessarily do that between tests if you  well if you destroy all the stuff and  completely close everything sure it  shuts down you don't actually  leak memory like if you have a memory  leak case for example where your program  would normally leak memory here and you  just close the program  it does release the memory but  you still have the memory leak that you  should fix but you won't notice it if  you just close the program so the point  here is i don't just close the program i  leave it running as it's right here it's  a global instead uh think of like a  playstation or an xbox or something  sometimes you just do you hit the reset  button right you don't you don't fully  power it off and cut the power and then  you know power back on instead you just  call a reset on all its core values and  have it reinitialize everything so i  wanted to shut down the sound devices i  want to shut down the graphics stuff i  want to shut down anything else like  that that is uh  needed initialized to get up and running  and uh this gets tricky with static  variables too the static variables don't  shut down on their own they stay in  scope forever essentially once they're  initialized they don't reinitialize so  you have to manually de-initialize them  so you gotta be really careful about  static values and there's some of those  in this engine to try to make things  more efficient for example when you load  a model  the importer is generally static so that  if you load like 10 models in a row it 